</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Impact of the Number of Training Goals</h3>

<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:41%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Impact of training dataset size on attack success rate (%). In this experiment, we set the maximum turn <math id="A4.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{max}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{max}}=5</annotation></semantics></math>, the branching factor to <math id="A4.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and group size <math id="A4.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=32</annotation></semantics></math>. We vary the number of training goals from 100 and 1200.
</figcaption>
<div id="A4.T7.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:195.6pt;height:49.2pt;vertical-align:-22.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="A4.T7.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A4.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
